Olta Ansible deployment
========================

Tested for current Ubuntu LTS releases. The role checks out
https://github.com/s4l1hs/olta, downloads the Go modules, and builds both
olta-campaign and olta-proxy from the selected `olta_version`.

1. Set the target host in `hosts`.
2. Review `roles/olta/vars/main.yml`, especially `olta_user`,
   `olta_campaign_domain`, and `olta_version`.
3. Run one of the following commands from this directory:

    ansible-playbook site.yml -i hosts -u root --private-key=private.key
    ansible-playbook site.yml -i hosts -u root --ask-pass
    ansible-playbook site.yml -i hosts -u ubuntu --become --ask-become-pass

Olta Campaign is enabled automatically. Olta Proxy is built and its systemd
unit is installed, but the unit remains disabled by default because its domain
and phishlet configuration must be completed first. Set
`olta_proxy_enabled: true` after preparing the proxy state.

The campaign listener binds to localhost by default; use an SSH tunnel to port
3333 for administration. The optional nginx frontend is disabled because it
would otherwise compete with Olta Proxy for ports 80/443 on a single host. Do
not set both `olta_nginx_enabled` and `olta_proxy_enabled` to true unless they
bind different IP addresses.

Required collections:

    ansible-galaxy collection install community.general community.crypto
